1
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,900
{\an8}Widgets lists everything a card can show, grouped by type.

2
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,250
{\an8}Phone widgets come straight from MOTO-HUB on your phone.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,900
{\an8}You can place them anywhere on your dash.

4
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:25,700
{\an8}Left panel and Right panel are the widget carousels you set up in the MOTO-HUB app.

5
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:30,200
{\an8}You choose their content on the phone.

6
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,100
{\an8}Select a card in the preview.

7
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,950
{\an8}The list shows the styles available for that widget.

8
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:43,375
{\an8}Pick a style. The speed, for example, can be Digits, Arc, Dial, Ring or Bubble.

9
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,300
{\an8}It works the same way for every widget.

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,500
{\an8}An empty preview means the card is too small for that style.

11
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,400
{\an8}Pick another style, or make the card bigger.

12
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:05,075
{\an8}If your dash doesn't have a widget yet, pick it from the list to add it.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,575
{\an8}To remove it, go back to Layout and delete its card.

14
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:18,825
{\an8}Select a widget, then click its small icon to see what a tap does.

15
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,400
{\an8}The map handles its own touches.

16
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:29,375
{\an8}Turn on Tap to zoom in Widgets, under Map, and a tap zooms to you. Turn it off to drag and pinch the map.

17
00:01:30,125 --> 00:01:32,675
{\an8}Other widgets let you pick the action.

18
00:01:33,675 --> 00:01:37,350
{\an8}For example, the weather widget can open your weather app.

19
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,000
{\an8}A widget can open a phone app, or a sub dash.
